# Used by `npm run dev` (Vite) only, NOT by the Docker Compose stack —
# points the dev server's browser bundle directly at a reachable
# OpenProcessor API origin, bypassing the nginx proxy Docker gets for
# free. Leave it commented out for `docker compose up`: compose passes it
# through to the browser bundle, which would then call this origin
# directly instead of the nginx proxy (F-48). Uncomment only for dev.
# PUBLIC_TRITON_API_URL=http://localhost:4603

# Top-bar wordmark + badge letters. Both optional — defaults to
# "Cropwright" / "CW" when unset. Override for a white-label deployment
# without touching source.
# PUBLIC_APP_NAME=Cropwright
# PUBLIC_APP_BADGE=CW

# Path prefix the backend serves its curation endpoints under.
#
# Defaults to /curation, OpenProcessor's API prefix. Leave unset unless
# the backend was started with a non-default OP_API_PREFIX. Must equal
# the backend's own OP_API_PREFIX — the API builds some URLs itself
# (region thumbnails) from its own prefix.
# PUBLIC_API_PREFIX=/curation

# --- The following are read by docker-compose.yml / docker-entrypoint.sh
# --- (the Docker deployment path), not by `npm run dev`.

# Where nginx proxies PUBLIC_API_PREFIX/* to — the OpenProcessor API
# container, reached by name over the shared docker network below.
# Defaults to the standard co-located OpenProcessor Docker Compose
# service name/port.
# API_UPSTREAM=http://op-api:8000

# The OpenProcessor API's docker network name (must already exist —
# `docker network ls`). Defaults to OpenProcessor's own default network.
# OP_DOCKER_NETWORK=openprocessor_triton_net

# Host port this instance publishes nginx on. Defaults to 5184.
# CROPWRIGHT_PORT=5184

# Container name for `docker compose up`. Defaults to "cropwright".
# Give a second, independent instance its own value (and its own
# `docker compose -p <project>`) so it doesn't collide with a running
# instance — see docker-compose.yml's header comment for a worked
# example.
# CROPWRIGHT_CONTAINER_NAME=cropwright

# Deployment-owned upload cap for /ingest (nginx client_max_body_size,
# in MB). Defaults to 256. Raise it for a deployment expecting very
# large batch uploads; docker-entrypoint.sh substitutes this into both
# nginx.conf and the served client config so the two never drift apart.
# CROPWRIGHT_INGEST_MAX_REQUEST_MB=256
